    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d620-a2">

                <pb facs="1136" n="1012" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg1012"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No.
                    97.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. de Giers to Mr.
                            Foster.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >St. Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1881-03-05"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 5,
                        1881</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have submitted to His Majesty the Emperor
                    the letter you addressed to me, in order to transmit to me the vote of the
                    Senate of the United States of America on the occasion of the horrible crime
                    under which has fallen the benefactor-sovereign, whom all Russia weeps for
                    to-day.</p>
                <p>My august master has been profoundly touched by this mark of respect for his
                    beloved father, and of sympathy with himself, coming from the high assembly of a
                    country for which the deceased Emperor always professed a sincere esteem and
                    warm friendship.</p>
                <p>It is a legacy which he leaves to the Emperor Alexander III, and which His
                    Majesty, in accord with the Russian nation, accepts from the bottom of his
                    heart.</p>
                <p>Will you, sir, give this assurance to the Senate of the United States, while
                    transmitting to it the thanks of my august master.</p>
                <p>Receive at the same time, &amp;c.</p>
                <closer><signed>GIERS.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
